// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING. STRICTEST TIER:
// Croatia sits with GREECE and the NETHERLANDS. Get this right.
// - Primary education (osnovna škola) is COMPULSORY for all children,
//   as a rule from about age six to fifteen, and the Ministry states
//   that the obligation is fulfilled through REGULAR ATTENDANCE at
//   primary school. Parental-choice homeschooling is NOT permitted
//   at primary level. Say so plainly and first.
// - THE ONLY EXCEPTION IS HEALTH-BASED AND STATE-ADMINISTERED:
//   "nastava u kući" — teaching at home — is a TEMPORARY form for
//   pupils who cannot attend because of major motor difficulties,
//   chronic illness, or impaired health, approved by the Ministry
//   and organised BY THE SCHOOL in cooperation with parents and
//   teachers, with subject or class examinations arranged. There is
//   also provision for release from regular attendance with distance
//   teaching, decided by the teachers' council on the proposal of the
//   school medicine physician. State these FACTUALLY ONLY. NEVER
//   position either as a pathway, never advise a family toward them.
// - REFORM IS DISCUSSED, NOT ENACTED. The Ministry has confirmed it
//   receives requests and that home education has been discussed in
//   the context of amendments to the Education Act, while noting
//   that preconditions would first have to be created and expert
//   opinion is divided. Report that accurately; predict nothing.
// - THE WINDOW — LOAD-BEARING HERE, AND WELL ATTESTED:
//   SECONDARY EDUCATION IN CROATIA IS NOT COMPULSORY. That is the
//   precise reason Croatian families who educate at home lawfully
//   do so at secondary level. So: compulsory attendance to about
//   fifteen, then the A-Level years entirely outside the obligation.
//   Use prominently — it is the single most useful fact on these
//   pages, and the contrast with the prohibited primary years is
//   what makes it worth stating carefully rather than loudly.
// - IZVANREDNI UČENICI: Croatian secondary schools recognise
//   external/part-time student status. Mention as something to
//   explore WITH THE SCHOOL for families who also want a Croatian
//   secondary qualification — always hedged, never asserted.
// SO: SUPPLEMENTARY IS THE DEFAULT during the compulsory years —
// the school enrolment carries the obligation, Cambridge runs
// alongside. Full-time Smartious is for the post-15 phase and for
// non-resident families under another country's framework.
// RESIDENCY: as in Greece, the obligation attaches to children
// resident in Croatia. Non-resident families follow their country
// of residence. State precisely; refer families to their own
// advisers. Relevant because Croatia's digital-nomad residence
// permit has drawn a genuinely new population since 2021.
// MARKET NOTE: the international tier is a Zagreb story — the
